  "pull_request": {
    "number": 149,
    "title": "Docs/lint naming convention",
    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds a documented lint naming convention to guide future lint additions.\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n\r\n- Added a dedicated \"Lint Naming Convention\" section to `CONTRIBUTING.md`\r\n- Documented recommendations for naming new lints:\r\n  - use lowercase snake_case\r\n  - prefer describing the detected code pattern over expressing a judgement\r\n  - use consistent `_in_loop` suffixes for loop-specific lints\r\n  - avoid the `soroban_` prefix unless needed to avoid ambiguity\r\n- Assessed the three existing lint names and documented them as accepted legacy names rather than recommending renaming, since lint names are part of the public API.\r\n\r\nCloses #111",
